3.0.0
Phase B of the subtraction programme: THIS is the release that deletes things, and it ships one release BEHIND the guards that make deleting safe — removals fail CLOSED where additions fail open, which is why the order was that way round and not a shortfall. B1 shrinks `AGENT_TEAM.md` from 1026 to 556 lines rather than deleting it, because deletion would destroy consumer content the toolkit itself told them to write into its PROJECT-CUSTOM region, and shrinking captures nearly all the saving at zero migration risk. The plan's ~150-line target is arithmetically unreachable and was NOT forced: its own named cut list leaves ~860, and reaching 150 requires deleting the Merge Protocol, the copy-paste snippets and the PROJECT_CONTEXT template — all three named as KEEP by the same plan, two of them gate-asserted. The real risk was never size but DANGLING CROSS-REFERENCES, so check 30 resolves every cited heading REPO-WIDE and reports wrong-filename separately from missing-section, because those have opposite remedies and a report saying only "dangling" actively invites the destructive fix — measured, the consumer who found the defect proposed two remedies and both were wrong. It arrived load-bearing: its first run was red on a defect SHIPPED IN ALL SIX VARIANTS, `AGENT_TEAM.md:76` citing `CLAUDE.md "Open Brain Context for Agents"` while the heading sat at `AGENT_TEAM.md:992`, 916 lines below the line pointing at it — the failure mode B1 exists to prevent had already occurred, in the opposite direction, with no shrink involved. Check 31 proves a 968 B PLANTED region survives a 98% deletion of the template part byte-exactly, planted because a census of three consumer repos found ZERO real region content and a guard that cannot fail proves nothing. B2 retires three agent names by ABSORPTION — `test-writer` into `tester`, `requirements-engineer` into `architect`, `doc-generator` into `coder` — never by rename, because the matcher regex and the skills case glob already generalise over the variant family and superset-under-an-existing-name works ONLY while the survivor keeps its name; a stale reference to a surviving name fails LOUDLY at spawn, a new name makes every consumer's prose stale at once, silently. "68 files → ~6" is wrong by a factor of ten: there are 13 distinct names and the 68 is a distribution artifact, so the honest outcome is 13 → 10, with the four domain coders surviving on a ROUTING-TABLE argument — the only measured routing table MANDATES `rust-coder` — never a usage one. Check 29 arm E asserts that existence proves nothing and MATCHING is the property, per pattern language, both directions; its first version was itself keyed on the thing under test and only deleting the guard found that. B3 exempts `SendMessage` from the agent budget, which had blocked five agent reports — a guard denying its own remedy — while keeping the ceiling untouched, and exempts it from COUNTING rather than merely from blocking, since a `-eq` threshold consumed by a report would silently skip the ceiling. Two B3 items are reported rather than implemented: the contract re-block cap already shipped in v2.2.2 with seven fixtures, and "demote" is defined nowhere and its only coherent reading contradicts the measurement that hook stderr does not reach the lead.
